Subject: [PATCH] viogpu helpers: read a pipe message inside its buffer

vgpusrv.exe and viogpuap.exe talk over a named pipe and each keeps a buffer
of 1024 wchar_t, 2048 bytes. DATA_BUFFER_SIZE had no parentheses, so
PipeServer::Read asked ReadFile for DATA_BUFFER_SIZE * sizeof(wchar_t) =
1024 * 2 * 2 = 4096 bytes: one message of more than 2048 bytes wrote past
the heap buffer of the service, which runs as SYSTEM. Both read loops
added the byte count of a piece to an index of wchar_t, so the second
piece of a message landed at twice its offset, and PipeClient::Read asked
for 2048 bytes at that index. Neither loop left a terminator: a message
that filled the buffer made GetData read past it.

Read a message through one function, VioGpuPipeReadMessage, that counts in
bytes, keeps the last unit of the buffer for the terminator and zeroes the
buffer behind the message. A message that does not fit is taken off the
pipe and dropped, and the buffer is then an empty string, which Run()
ignores. The function is in a header with no include:
tests/kmd/pipe_bounds_test.cpp of the package compiles it on the build
host. DATA_BUFFER_SIZE gets its parentheses.

Card #757, finding F9 of the win3d driver review. docs/acceptance/C757.md
has the proof.
---
